{
  "about": "Pattern unrolling vectors (docs/07-phase-6.md, \u0022Pattern regions\u0022): Anode.Model\u0027s PatternUnroller computes these; the editor\u0027s must match them exactly. Ticks are relative to the region\u0027s start (960 per quarter note). A row walks positions k = 0, 1, \u2026 every stepTicks (its own, else the pattern\u0027s) while k*stepTicks \u003C lengthTicks; its step: forward k mod L, reverse L-1-(k mod L), ping-pong c = k mod (2L-2), c \u003C L ? c : 2L-2-c (L = 1: step 0), random floor(draw(seed, region, row, \u0022r\u0022, k) * L). An on step plays unless chance \u003C 1 and draw(seed, region, row, k mod L, k div L) \u003E= chance. Its start: k*stepTicks, \u002B swing*120 when that is 240 mod 480, \u002B offset*stepTicks, at least 0 (unrounded). Its gate gate*stepTicks splits into repeats notes from round(start \u002B i*gate/n) to round(start \u002B (i\u002B1)*gate/n), at least a tick; dropped at or after the region\u0027s end, cut there. Pitch: the row\u0027s note (pad rows too); a chord degree d plays the triad of degrees d, d\u002B2, d\u002B4 of the key at the step (major or natural minor), its root in 60\u202671. Sorted by tick, pitch, row order. draw(seed, region, row, step, pass): the string seed:region:row:step:pass (seed and pass in decimal), FNV-1a 32-bit over its UTF-16 code units (h = 2166136261; h ^= unit; h *= 16777619), then h ^= h \u003E\u003E\u003E 16; h *= 0x85EBCA6B; h ^= h \u003E\u003E\u003E 13; h *= 0xC2B2AE35; h ^= h \u003E\u003E\u003E 16 (32-bit unsigned throughout), divided by 2^32.",
